# WorkflowHub

Downloads Galaxy workflows from WorkflowHub and finds which tool connnects to which, to compare with the literature graph.

download_workflowhub.py gets the metadata of every workflow on WorkflowHub, then downloads the RO-Crate (zip) of each Galaxy workflow and takes out its .ga file. Files already downloaded are skipped, so it can be stopped and run again. Add --limit 5 to test on 5.

To run:
```
python3 directed-graph/workflowhub/download_workflowhub.py
```


```
data/                     (git-ignored)
├── index.json            all workflow IDs
├── meta/<id>.json        metadata per workflow (all types)
├── crates/               RO-Crate zips (Galaxy only)
├── ga/<id>_v<version>/   .ga files from the crates
├── workflows.csv         one row per workflow
├── galaxy_pairs.csv      tool A feeds tool B, per workflow
├── galaxy_edges.csv      same pairs, counted over workflows
└── galaxy_tools.csv      tools and how many workflows use them
```

Tools are named by ToolShed name (e.g. `megahit`), not yet bio.tools ID.